{
  "id": 329385384,
  "iid": 17383,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "ieee1905: decode Assoc Request body from Client Cap Report TLV",
  "description": "Hi,\n\nThis is the last of my updates to the ieee1905 dissector (at least for the moment).\n\nDecoding the association request received in client cap report is very useful in practice.\n\nThe only problem is that the EM standard has an oversight so you cannot know what the received data is (assoc request or reassoc request frame).\n\nAs Assoc Request is more occuring in practice, it attempts to decode that.\n\n!! In a SW Product using this TLV the SSID is known and can be used to get IE in both assoc/reassoc case.\n\nExample:\n[tlv_91_client_capability_report.pcap](/uploads/b1a36b6a5913d72d31cd53e80d1a08df/tlv_91_client_capability_report.pcap)\n\n![client_cap_report](/uploads/01ef83c03169a8aa6301cdd4f433e6c8/client_cap_report.png)",
